WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.938
[music playing]

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.073
- There you go that's good.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.007
- Anyway.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.576
- Yeah.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.945
- Keegan-Michael Key and I are
closing in on our extraction

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:15.482
point, but first we've got to
use a diagonal line to descend

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.585
a 250 foot Icelandic waterfall.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.519
- That's it.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.453
That's it.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.721
Now keep your legs
down, legs down.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.089
[groans]

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.290
- Holy [bleep].

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.594
- Have a check out.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.428
Are there seagulls?

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.763
I bet there'd be seagulls there.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.901
- There's a baby
seagull right there.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.803
It's amazing.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.105
He doesn't know what the
hell I'm doing here, but--

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:42.442
[laughs] Oh my God.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.977
- Remember, don't look down.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:44.611
- OK.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.445
- OK.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.513
I'm going to start lowering you.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.213
Here you go.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.952
[music playing]

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:59.125
- [laughing] Just me and baby
seagull sitting on the cliff

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:03.430
[music playing]

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:06.166
- Look at the power of it.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.100
- Well done, Keegan.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.568
Good job.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.602
Almost there.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.637
Last bit.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.641
- [whoops] [chuckles]

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:18.378
[music playing]

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.747
- We said we were going to
get someplace really fast.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.815
That was pretty fast.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:22.749
- OK.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.951
Time to go and join him.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.886
- Coming off the
waterfall, as I was

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:31.491
going down right to the edge,
I'm like, what are we doing?

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.993
And the next thing I
know, I'm just in midair.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.864
But what a view.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:43.102
[laughing] Whoo!

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.070
That was amazing.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.606
You came down really fast.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.440
- Yeah.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.475
Well, it's called hot gloves.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.943
- Oh, you got hot gloves.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.877
Oh, you got hot--

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:51.811
- Good job, though.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:52.645
- Oh, thanks, man.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.379
Unbelievable.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.280
- Yeah, it's amazing.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.482
- Unbelievable.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.016
- How can we get
around the back of it?

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.051
Look.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.253
- That would be amazing, yeah.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.188
- So we're at the
bottom of this now.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.690
Keegan is pumped.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:08.194
It looks like we might be
able to sneak a little route

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.929
around the back
of the flow, which

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:13.366
would be pretty epic to see.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.234
Wow.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.134
There you go.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.470
- It's amazing.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.472
- Like a little hidden
grotto, isn't it?

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.441
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:24.043
I love the sound it makes
when it hits the rocks.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.012
It's as if it was
planned, you know?

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.714
It's completely untouched.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.784
[music playing]

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.520
- So that's nature at its best.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.221
- I've never seen
anything like that.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.556
To see the little gulls!

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.392
It's so funny to watch
them, like, who is this?

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.126
- Yeah.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.094
- It's just-- but I just--

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.395
I don't know what it is.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.664
It's just communing
with another life form.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.632
- Yeah.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.467
- You said something
earlier about

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.903
you just kind of see
yourself-- nature

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.571
is a mirror for yourself.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.040
It's really-- that
really-- that--

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.209
I mean, coming down
the side of that cliff

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.677
was exciting and exhilarating.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.045
But seeing those gulls?

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.414
Like, that was something I never
expected to see in my life,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.081
you know?

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:02.849
And it's just great.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.083
It was amazing.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.685
- It's like, for me
almost, you start

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:08.321
out the journey with the weight
of the world on your shoulders.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.289
- A little bit, yeah.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.523
- And you're finishing it.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.191
I love the way it's
the little things,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.728
like nature, birds, and animals
that lifts your spirits.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.131
- What would have happened
if I just said no no no no,

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.432
I can't do that.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.000
Then I wouldn't--
you know, I would

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.602
have never seen those gulls.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.904
What would have happened if I
had said no no no, you're cool.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.005
You have the spider.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.040
Like, just do it, Keegan.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.341
What happens if you just do it?

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:28.875
- Yeah.

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.276
- You know?

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.911
- Well, the stuff we fear
is itself often never

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.946
as bad once you face it.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:33.880
- Exactly.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:34.514
Exactly.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.882
Yeah.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.216
- Well, that's an inspiring
message, and you've lived it.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.184
More importantly,
you've lived it.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:38.818
- I've lived it, right.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:39.752
Right.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.820
- OK, we're pushing on.

